flowchart TB
    subgraph BAD["the clock read INSIDE the method"]
        direction TB
        B1["store.get('k')"] --> B2["expiry &lt;= time.time()?"]
        B2 --> B3["to test expiry at all, the test<br/>has to really sleep for 10 seconds"]:::bad
    end
    subgraph GOOD["the clock passed IN as a parameter"]
        direction TB
        G1["store.get('k', now=109)"] --> G2["expiry &lt;= now?"]
        G2 --> G3["assert alive at 109, dead at 110 —<br/>instant, deterministic, nothing sleeps"]:::good
    end
    BAD --> WHY["Same logic either way; the only question is who supplies 'now'.<br/>Injecting it lets the grader replay any timeline it likes, and<br/>'inject the clock' is a habit interviewers actively look for."]
    GOOD --> WHY
    WHY --> MONO["Durations are a separate matter: time.monotonic() only ever moves<br/>forward, while time.time() can jump backwards when NTP corrects it."]:::note
    classDef bad fill:#ffe0e0,stroke:#8a1c1c,color:#1f2328
    classDef good fill:#dafbe1,stroke:#1a7f37,color:#1f2328
    classDef note fill:#fff8e6,stroke:#d4a72c,color:#4d2d00
